><text color="#9643FC" creationdate="D:20250626112558+10'00'" flags="print,nozoom,norotate" inreplyto="87a72c8f-b5d3-4c46-b889-a9242e71f98c" date="D:20250626112558+10'00'" name="0d329985-9698-4b0a-add2-3580ff0a0521" icon="Comment" page="5" rect="306.131226,468.696136,330.131226,492.696136" subject="Sticky Note" title="alexd"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>The implementation of a systems-based secondary injury prevention intervention provides preliminary positive findings in reducing HSI and time-loss groin injury burdens in a cohort of male professional football players, when compared with a control period. This study provides practitioners with a practical framework that can be applied in male professional football, that is acceptable to players and coaches, without interfering with normal team schedules.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="5" rect="595.276001,400.696136,779.276001,492.696136"
/></text
></annots
><f href="10.1016_j.ptsp.2024.08.003.pdf"
/><ids original="EA7A1A226D6EE006478E485D56851A2D" modified="A0E168F75F004F29865F2C692F8B9D1D"
/></xfdf
>